      {
         "id": "d",
         "prompt": "Find the value of \\( F(2) \\). Then use the series from part (b) to find the exact value of \\( \\displaystyle\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{(n + 1)\\,2^{n}} \\).",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "F(2) = 2 + 4\\ln 2, \\qquad \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{(n + 1)2^{n}} = 2\\ln 2",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Evaluate the closed form at x = 2.",
               "latex": "F(2) = 2 - 4\\ln\\frac{1}{2} = 2 + 4\\ln 2"
            },
            {
               "text": "Evaluate the series at x = 2.",
               "latex": "F(2) = 2 + \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{2^{n+1}}{(n + 1)4^{n}} = 2 + 2\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{(n + 1)2^{n}}"
            },
            {
               "text": "Equate the two and solve.",
               "latex": "2\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{(n + 1)2^{n}} = 4\\ln 2"
            },
            {
               "text": "The value of the sum.",
               "latex": "\\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{(n + 1)2^{n}} = 2\\ln 2"
            }
